<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>WUT 2.0 Guide</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <%- include('partials_header') %>
  <main class="container cards-page wut-guide">
    <section class="card page-title cards-title">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">FAQ & Tutorial</p><h1>How to Play WUT 2.0</h1><p>Build a legal deck, outplay your opponent, and turn real WCPL performances into Fantasy Points.</p></div>
      <div class="cards-title-actions"><a class="button-link ghost" href="/cards">WUT Hub</a><% if (cardsOpen) { %><a class="button-link" href="/cards/collection">Collection</a><% } %></div>
    </section>

    <nav class="card wut-guide-nav" aria-label="Guide sections">
      <a href="#start">Quick Start</a><a href="#cards">Cards</a><a href="#decks">Decks</a><a href="#matches">Matches</a><a href="#scoring">Scoring</a><a href="#trinkets">Trinkets</a><a href="#economy">Shop & Rewards</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a>
    </nav>

    <div class="wut-guide-grid">
      <section class="card" id="start">
        <p class="eyebrow">Five-minute version</p><h2>Quick Start</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Join WUT and open your starter bundle: five unique Common cards (2F / 2D / 1G), two Common trinkets, 1,000 WUT Coins, and a free Standard pack.</li>
          <li>Open the free pack in the Shop, then visit Decks to build a lineup and assign trinkets.</li>
          <li>Build and save an exact-size deck if you want to play Constructed Arena. The default is eight cards.</li>
          <li>Enter Draft Arena to mini-draft shared packs, or select a saved deck and enter Constructed Arena.</li>
          <li>Take turns assigning cards to F1, F2, D1, D2, and G. Add optional boosts, lock your choices, then reveal the final score.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="card" id="cards">
        <p class="eyebrow">Your collection</p><h2>Reading a Card</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>MP</strong> is the number of WUT matches in which that copy has scored. <strong>FP/M</strong> is its average Fantasy Points per WUT match.</li>
          <li>Click a collection card to flip it. Its back shows the season stat line and accumulated WUT results.</li>
          <li>Rarity is calculated within position. S1 and S2 share a pool; S3 has its own pool and requires at least six games to enter the rankings.</li>
          <li><strong>Power = card rarity value + trinket Power.</strong> Cards are Common 1, Uncommon 2, Rare 3, Epic 4, Legendary 5, and Mythic 6. Trinkets add Common +0, Uncommon +0.5, Rare +1, Epic +1.5, or Legendary +2.5. Boosts add no Power.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="card" id="decks">
        <p class="eyebrow">Prepare before queueing</p><h2>Deck Building</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Deck size:</strong> normal WUT decks require exactly eight unique cards by default. Admins can configure the size.</li>
          <li><strong>Positions:</strong> every deck must include at least 2F / 2D / 1G.</li>
          <li><strong>Top lineup cap:</strong> your highest-Power 2F / 2D / 1G combination must not exceed the configured cap. The default is 15 Power and includes trinket Power.</li>
          <li>Draft Events have their own deck size and top-lineup Power cap in the draft preset, so special formats can raise or lower the cap.</li>
          <li>Constructed Arena snapshots your selected deck when you queue. Later collection changes do not alter that active match.</li>
          <li>Draft Arena has no deck-size or position minimum. You pick one item from each shared pack, then assign drafted trinkets before locking.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="card" id="matches">
        <p class="eyebrow">Asynchronous head-to-head</p><h2>Playing a Match</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Constructed Arena is best-of-three. Game 1 starts with a coin flip and the winner chooses who plays first. In game 2, the game-1 first player goes second. If game 3 is needed, the better combined FP differential from games 1 and 2 chooses first or second; tied differential falls back to a coin flip.</li>
          <li>Each turn asks you to commit the maximum legal number of cards up to the turn cap.</li>
          <li>Lineups use 2F / 2D / 1G. A card must match the position of its chosen slot.</li>
          <li>Draft Arena prep has one two-hour timer. If you do not lock your draft and trinket assignments before it expires, you forfeit.</li>
          <li>After an opponent fills a matching slot, your response can be at most one Power higher by default.</li>
          <li>If you have no legal card for any open slot, you are done committing cards for that match. Your opponent can keep filling slots; your empty slots score 0.</li>
          <li>You may commit consumable boosts up to your lineup's Boost Load. Standard load is 5; some Booster Cables increase it.</li>
          <li>A committed turn is permanent. Each player has two active hours per turn; the clock pauses during the configured overnight window.</li>
          <li>When no player has legal plays remaining, open the match to watch the slot-by-slot scoring reveal.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="card" id="scoring">
        <p class="eyebrow">Three unique performances</p><h2>Scoring & Chemistry</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Each card rolls three different eligible games from its printed season. The detailed scoring view can show every rolled game's stat line and FP.</li>
          <li>Goals, assists, shots, hits, blocks, goalie saves, save percentage, and shutouts feed the configured scoring table.</li>
          <li>Cards need the <strong>same team and same season</strong> for chemistry. Two, three, four, or five matching cards earn the configured chemistry bonus.</li>
          <li>The reveal lists base statistics, boosts, chemistry, and trinket effects separately so every FP change can be traced.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="card wut-guide-wide" id="trinkets">
        <p class="eyebrow">Permanent build identity</p><h2>Trinkets</h2>
        <% const guideRarities = ['common', 'uncommon', 'rare', 'epic', 'legendary']; const captainPatchEffects = wutConfig?.trinketEffects?.team_crest || {}; %>
        <p>Trinkets add a rarity-scaled effect and up to 2.5 Power. A Common trinket adds no Power but still provides its effect. Trinkets are assigned inside a deck and can be changed freely before saving.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Roll control:</strong> Lucky Charm, Safety Net, and Glass Skates.</li>
          <li><strong>Scoring builds:</strong> Specialist, Generalist, Underdog Patch, First Strike, and Counterpunch Gloves.</li>
          <li><strong>Boost and chemistry builds:</strong> Booster Cable, Captain's Patch, and Journeyman.</li>
          <li><strong>Counterplay:</strong> Hex Charm, Warding Charm, Siphon Stone, and Zebra Stripes.</li>
          <li>Only Specialist and Generalist are skater-only. Up to two Captain's Patches can be active in a lineup; the second one played becomes an Assistant Captain and receives 50% of the Patch benefit.</li>
          <li><strong>Current Captain's Patch:</strong> <%= guideRarities.map(rarity => `${wutTitleCase(rarity)}: ${wutTrinketDescription({ family: 'team_crest', rarity, effect: captainPatchEffects[rarity] })}`).join(' ') %></li>
        </ul>
        <div class="wut-trinket-encyclopedia" data-trinket-encyclopedia>
          <div class="cards-section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Current balance</p><h3>Trinket Effects</h3></div></div>
          <div class="wut-trinket-encyclopedia-icons" role="tablist" aria-label="Trinkets">
            <% Object.keys(WUT_TRINKET_ICONS).forEach((family, index) => { %>
              <button type="button" class="wut-trinket-encyclopedia-pick <%= index === 0 ? 'is-selected' : '' %>" data-trinket-family-pick="<%= family %>" role="tab" aria-selected="<%= index === 0 ? 'true' : 'false' %>" title="<%= wutTrinketName(family) %>"><span class="wut-trinket-icon"><%= WUT_TRINKET_ICONS[family] %></span><small><%= wutTrinketName(family) %></small></button>
            <% }) %>
          </div>
          <% Object.keys(WUT_TRINKET_ICONS).forEach((family, index) => { %>
            <div class="wut-trinket-encyclopedia-panel" data-trinket-family-panel="<%= family %>" <%= index === 0 ? '' : 'hidden' %>>
              <h3><span><%= WUT_TRINKET_ICONS[family] %></span> <%= wutTrinketName(family) %></h3>
              <div class="wut-trinket-rarity-list">
                <% guideRarities.forEach(rarity => { const effect = wutConfig?.trinketEffects?.[family]?.[rarity]; %>
                  <div class="wut-trinket-rarity-row"><span class="wut-trinket-icon tier-<%= rarity %>"><%= WUT_TRINKET_ICONS[family] %></span><div><strong class="tier-text-<%= rarity %>"><%= wutTitleCase(rarity) %> · +<%= wutConfig?.trinketPowerValues?.[rarity] ?? 0 %> Power</strong><p><%= wutTrinketDescription({ family, rarity, effect }) %></p></div></div>
                <% }) %>
              </div>
            </div>
          <% }) %>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="card" id="economy">
        <p class="eyebrow">WUT Coins stay inside WUT</p><h2>Shop & Rewards</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Every player pack contains three unique players and two boosts. Boost packs contain only boost consumables, including a configurable high-rarity guarantee.</li>
          <li>A purchased pack must be revealed and claimed before another pack can be bought.</li>
          <li>Each player has a separate three-offer Trinket Shop. It refreshes automatically at midnight Pacific Time.</li>
          <li>Completed matches award WUT Coins. Winners receive more; a timeout loser receives none.</li>
          <li>Mission rewards are not automatic. Return to the WUT Hub and press Claim.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="card" id="faq">
        <p class="eyebrow">Common questions</p><h2>FAQ</h2>
        <details open><summary>Why is a card missing while I build a deck?</summary><p>A card already assigned to the deck is hidden below.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What happens if I run out of legal plays?</summary><p>You are done committing cards for that match. Any unfilled lineup slots remain empty and score 0.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Are boosts permanent?</summary><p>No. Boosts are consumables committed to a match. If an administrator voids a stuck match, its committed boosts are released.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Do two cards from the same team but different seasons get chemistry?</summary><p>No. Both team and printed season must match. Legendary Journeyman is the special exception that can adopt any team-season identity currently in play.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Why did my trinket do nothing?</summary><p>Many effects have a trigger condition, may be weakened by Warding Charm or Zebra Stripes, or may lose an order-of-play contest. The detailed reveal identifies triggered and missed effects.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Where are my decks?</summary><p>Open Collection and choose Decks. The main WUT Hub stays focused on missions, matchmaking, and active games.</p></details>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <script>
    document.querySelectorAll('[data-trinket-encyclopedia]').forEach(encyclopedia => {
      encyclopedia.addEventListener('click', event => {
        const pick = event.target.closest('[data-trinket-family-pick]');
        if (!pick) return;
        const family = pick.dataset.trinketFamilyPick;
        encyclopedia.querySelectorAll('[data-trinket-family-pick]').forEach(button => {
          const selected = button === pick;
          button.classList.toggle('is-selected', selected);
          button.setAttribute('aria-selected', selected ? 'true' : 'false');
        });
        encyclopedia.querySelectorAll('[data-trinket-family-panel]').forEach(panel => { panel.hidden = panel.dataset.trinketFamilyPanel !== family; });
      });
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
